WEBVTT

00:12:27.537 --> 00:12:32.996
I must answer this question. So so what
how would you describe what's going on?

00:12:32.996 --> 00:12:35.121
You've got something that has
read the entire Internet,

00:12:35.121 --> 00:12:37.662
essentially all of Wikipedia, etc. We've

00:12:37.662 --> 00:12:41.287
read something that's read like a small
fraction of a random sampling of

00:12:41.287 --> 00:12:44.579
the Internet. We will eventually train
something that has read as much of

00:12:44.579 --> 00:12:47.621
the Internet or more of the Internet
than we've done right now.

00:12:47.871 --> 00:12:49.371
But we have a very long way to go.

00:12:49.371 --> 00:12:50.371
I mean, we're still, I think,

00:12:50.371 --> 00:12:54.704
relative to what we will have operated
at quite small scale with quite small

00:12:54.746 --> 00:13:01.871
eyes. But what is happening is there is
a model that is ingesting lots of text